<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!-- The fire ground for the cooperation scenario: a 20 x 20 m stand of timber.

     uav_bushfire's world is 12 x 12, which is the right size for three
     aircraft working alone. It is too small for this one, and the reason is
     the ground fleet rather than the air fleet. A Scout is 0.93 m long and
     drives at 0.9 m/s; in a 12 m arena it is never more than a few seconds
     from anywhere, so the tenders were always already where they needed to be
     and the logistics half of the scenario cost nothing. There was also
     nowhere to put the dam that was not either among the fires or on top of a
     launch point.

     At 20 x 20 the numbers mean something. The dam sits in the far corner at
     (8.5, 8.5), a 12 m drive from the far side of the stand - a real errand
     for a tender, and long enough that leaving for it at the wrong moment is a
     decision with a cost. Fires are lit within +-7.0, so a drone can be a 14 m
     transit from its next job, which is more than one tank of water.

     Eighteen trees rather than eight, on three rings, so the density stays
     about what it was: an arena three times the area with the same eight
     trunks is open ground, and the reactive avoidance both fleets are built
     around would never fire. Trees are kept clear of the dam corner and of the
     three launch points on the y axis.

     Everything else is uav_bushfire's world unchanged, including the reasons.
     Trunks are 3 m and the firebreak walls are 3 m, both to stop the obvious
     cheat - an aircraft's answer to an obstacle is to go over it, and if it
     can, the avoidance never runs. Canopies carry NO collision geometry, only
     a visual: the laser is a horizontal plane, so a solid canopy would be an
     obstacle the drone can hit and has no sensor able to see. Tops a rotor
     passes through keep the picture honest.

     Generated rather than written by hand, so the obstacle list
     incident_controller is given comes from the same numbers - a fire lit
     inside a trunk is an aircraft grinding against bark until the reignite
     timer moves it, and nothing checks. -->
<sdf version="1.6">
  <world name="default">

    <include><uri>model://sun</uri></include>
    <include><uri>model://ground_plane</uri></include>

    <scene>
      <ambient>0.6 0.6 0.6 1</ambient>
      <shadows>false</shadows>
    </scene>

    <physics type="ode">
      <max_step_size>0.001</max_step_size>
      <real_time_update_rate>1000</real_time_update_rate>
    </physics>

    <model name="tree_00">
      <static>true</static><pose>4.00 0.00 1.5 0 0 0</pose>
      <link name="link">
        <collision name="c"><geometry><cylinder><radius>0.35</radius><length>3.0</length></cylinder></geometry></collision>
        <visual name="v"><geometry><cylinder><radius>0.35</radius><length>3.0</length></cylinder></geometry>
          <material><ambient>0.18 0.12 0.07 1</ambient><diffuse>0.34 0.23 0.14 1</diffuse></material></visual>
        <visual name="canopy">
          <pose>0 0 1.75 0 0 0</pose>
          <geometry><sphere><radius>0.95</radius></sphere></geometry>
          <material><ambient>0.08 0.16 0.07 1</ambient><diffuse>0.16 0.34 0.14 1</diffuse></material>
        </visual>
      </link>
    </model>
    <model name="tree_01">
      <static>true</static><pose>2.00 3.46 1.5 0 0 0</pose>
      <link name="link">
        <collision name="c"><geometry><cylinder><radius>0.35</radius><length>3.0</length></cylinder></geometry></collision>
